test.yaml:11:14: "twine upload" publishes to PyPI with the long-lived credential TWINE_PASSWORD. prefer trusted publishing with pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:14:14: "twine upload" publishes to PyPI. prefer trusted publishing with pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:15:14: "uv publish" publishes to PyPI. prefer trusted publishing with pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:16:14: "uvx twine upload" publishes to PyPI. prefer trusted publishing with pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:17:14: "poetry publish" publishes to PyPI. prefer trusted publishing with pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:18:14: "cargo publish" publishes to crates.io with the long-lived credential CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN. prefer trusted publishing with rust-lang/crates-io-auth-action and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:19:14: "npm publish" publishes to npm with the long-lived credential NODE_AUTH_TOKEN. prefer trusted publishing: configure the trusted publisher of the package on npmjs.com and grant the permission "id-token: write", then no token is needed [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:22:14: "pnpm publish" publishes to npm. prefer trusted publishing: configure the trusted publisher of the package on npmjs.com and grant the permission "id-token: write", then no token is needed [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:23:14: "yarn npm publish" publishes to npm. prefer trusted publishing: configure the trusted publisher of the package on npmjs.com and grant the permission "id-token: write", then no token is needed [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:24:14: "gem push" publishes to RubyGems with the long-lived credential GEM_HOST_API_KEY. prefer trusted publishing with rubygems/release-gem and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:27:14: "bundle exec gem push" publishes to RubyGems. prefer trusted publishing with rubygems/release-gem and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:28:14: "dotnet nuget push" publishes to NuGet. prefer trusted publishing with NuGet/login and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:32:21: action "pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish@76f52bc884231f62b9a034ebfe128415bbaabdfc" publishes to PyPI but is given a password (input "password") instead of using trusted publishing. prefer trusted publishing with pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:35:22: action "rubygems/configure-rubygems-credentials@bc6dd217f8a4f919d6835fcfefd470ef821f5c44" publishes to RubyGems but is given an API token (input "api-token") instead of using trusted publishing. prefer trusted publishing with rubygems/release-gem and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:38:36: action "rubygems/release-gem@9e85cb11501bebc2ae661c1500176316d3987059" publishes to RubyGems but is told not to set up trusted publishing (input "setup-trusted-publisher") instead of using trusted publishing. prefer trusted publishing with rubygems/release-gem and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:42:24: action "actions/setup-node@39370e3970a6d050c480ffad4ff0ed4d3fdee5af" publishes to npm but sends a token with every request to npm (input "always-auth") instead of using trusted publishing. prefer trusted publishing: configure the trusted publisher of the package on npmjs.com and grant the permission "id-token: write", then no token is needed [use-trusted-publishing]
test.yaml:73:14: "cargo publish" publishes to crates.io with the long-lived credential CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN. prefer trusted publishing with rust-lang/crates-io-auth-action and the permission "id-token: write" [use-trusted-publishing]
